        "question": "What is the most frequent mistake students make regarding the transition to alumni: how the college date stays with you?",
        "answer": "The most common error is making assumptions without explicit, open communication. When students avoid honest conversations due to fear of awkwardness or conflict, minor friction compounds into major resentment. Establishing mutual expectations early prevents unnecessary misunderstandings. Supporting each other through project research deadlines, practicing patience with supervisor stress, and discussing future plans openly ensures relationship resilience."
