        "question": "What is the most frequent mistake students make regarding from the college date to real life: the optimal 5-day roadmap?",
        "answer": "The most common error is making assumptions without explicit, open communication. When students avoid honest conversations due to fear of awkwardness or conflict, minor friction compounds into major resentment. Establishing mutual expectations early prevents unnecessary misunderstandings. Using engaging, respectful conversation openers, keeping voice notes authentic, and moving promptly to real-world campus meetups ensures digital courting success."
